  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "Recent deepTools4 and CLIPittyClip releases report benchmarked speed-ups and single-command workflows for established genomic analysis steps.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these items is re-engineering of established analysis steps for speed, automation, and usability rather than introducing new statistical methods. deepTools4 rewrites core functions of a genomic sequencing analysis suite, reporting benchmarked speed-ups and updated visualization. MAUDE-Py reimplements the MAUDE probabilistic framework in Python for sorting-based pooled CRISPR screens, adding automated baselines and null sampling. CLIPittyClip packages CLIP sequencing analysis as a local single-command pipeline from raw FASTQ to peak matrices and crosslink sites, with a 27-fold faster Python crosslink step (CLink). RSMViewer, a PyMOL plugin, addresses a downstream step by enabling batch visualization and superimposition of RNA structural motif instances. Tycholyzer combines, normalizes and fits nanoDSF fluorescence traces to derive melting temperatures. The items span distinct domains, so this thread is dominant rather than shared by every item.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-16"
}
